1
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:53,030
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,700
[Episode 32]

3
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:13,920
You've been questioned all day.

4
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,250
Are you holding up okay?

5
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,560
Careful. It's hot.

6
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,360
Thank you.

7
00:01:18,289 --> 00:01:19,980
All of this is standard procedure.

8
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:21,110
Don't overthink it.

9
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:22,380
Just be cooperative.

10
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,000
If you've missed or omitted something,

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,920
just tell me.

12
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:29,789
[Forensic Investigation Room]

13
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,280
Last month—

14
00:01:32,539 --> 00:01:33,680
I forget which day—

15
00:01:34,370 --> 00:01:37,430
I treated the cement factory's
sales managers to dinner,

16
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,960
after which, I went with them
to sing kareoke.

17
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:42,840
Three Eyes happened to be on duty
that night.

18
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,090
I saw him in the lobby.

19
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,310
We said hi to each other.

20
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,080
That was the last time we talked.

21
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:53,580
I understand.

22
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,400
You must be feeling awful right now.

23
00:01:58,140 --> 00:01:59,810
You grew up with him,

24
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,160
and married his sister later.

25
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,920
Besides his mother and sister,

26
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,010
you are the closest to him.

27
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:11,360
If even you hadn't noticed
anything wrong with him,

28
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,310
then nobody else

29
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:13,910
would have.

30
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:23,650
I used to think of myself

31
00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:25,300
as his best friend.

32
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,740
I loved his sister for many years.

33
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,520
This time, when I came back
from the forest farm,

34
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:45,270
I thought I'd return
after a few months' rest.

35
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,200
It was not until

36
00:02:48,410 --> 00:02:49,780
I ran into Three Eyes did I know

37
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:52,040
that his sister had fallen severely ill.

38
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:59,030
I didn't marry her out of pity.

39
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:01,090
I truly loved her.

40
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,250
When we got married,

41
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:07,590
Three Eyes was the happiest of all.

42
00:03:07,590 --> 00:03:09,150
He kept calling me Brother-in-Law.

43
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:09,950
It sounded...

44
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:11,410
so affectionate.

45
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,620
He is

46
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,590
foolishly honest

47
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:19,670
and slow on the uptake.

48
00:03:22,130 --> 00:03:24,060
Later, when Chen Hong got pregnant

49
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:27,380
and Hao Jie went to Shanghai,

50
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,910
he finally found out
my affair with Chen Hong.

51
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,340
He blamed me.

52
00:03:46,850 --> 00:03:48,980
He blamed me for betraying his sister.

53
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,810
But Chen Hong saved her life.

54
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:59,280
Given that, we both felt awkward
and uneasy when we met up again

55
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,010
thereafter.

56
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:05,720
Eventually, we cut off contact
with each other.

57
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:11,840
So where do you think

58
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:14,130
he can possibly be right now?

59
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,360
I'm also eager to know where he is.

60
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:22,600
I've never been able to reach his sister

61
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,250
since she went to Shanghai.

62
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,480
I really want to ask him

63
00:04:30,390 --> 00:04:31,500
how she is doing now

64
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,520
and if she has been cured.

65
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:57,090
Here, sign this.

66
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,360
Any findings?

67
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:05,390
The forensic report is in.

68
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,070
The dagger is the murder weapon.

69
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:08,870
We've issued an arrest warrant.

70
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:14,450
We'll be leaving then.

71
00:05:48,409 --> 00:05:55,659
[Wanted]

72
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:12,580
[Half a month ago]

73
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,720
Yang?

74
00:06:43,450 --> 00:06:44,690
Sit down.

75
00:06:44,690 --> 00:06:45,450
Yang,

76
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:46,380
open your mouth.

77
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:47,500
Open up.

78
00:06:55,659 --> 00:06:56,450
What's this?

79
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:57,720
Chicken butt.

80
00:06:58,330 --> 00:06:59,300
With poop on it.

81
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,440
This chicken

82
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:14,000
must have had diarrhea before it died.

83
00:07:21,950 --> 00:07:23,620
Do you remember Mr. Ji,

84
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,200
your homeroom teacher who taught math?

85
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,300
You mean Baldy Ji!

86
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:28,890
That was Baldy Ji.

87
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:29,890
Yes, exactly.

88
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:31,720
His glasses were as thick
as the bottom of a beer bottle.

89
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,150
Right.

90
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:33,920
Oh my.

91
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,920
One time, you were caught smoking
in the restroom

92
00:07:37,180 --> 00:07:39,310
by a teacher from another class.

93
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:40,450
Mr. Ji told you to get a parent
to the school,

94
00:07:40,450 --> 00:07:41,450
or he wouldn't let you go home.

95
00:07:41,450 --> 00:07:41,870
Yes.

96
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:44,780
So you asked me to pretend
to be your dad, right?

97
00:07:49,250 --> 00:07:51,050
You were a real badass back then,

98
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:52,450
taller than me by a head.

99
00:07:52,450 --> 00:07:53,010
I was.

100
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:54,159
You...

101
00:07:54,659 --> 00:07:56,890
You asked a bulky fool...
What was his name?

102
00:07:56,890 --> 00:07:57,600
Let me think.

103
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,930
To lend you his glasses.

104
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,000
He was called Four Eyes.

105
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:00,600
Yes!

106
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,660
He was nicknamed Four Eyes.

107
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:02,740
You borrowed glasses from Four Eyes,

108
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:04,600
put on a hat, and came to my school.

109
00:08:05,010 --> 00:08:07,340
Once you got to Baldy Ji's office,
he began

110
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:09,430
lecturing you
and it went on for 30 minutes.

111
00:08:09,430 --> 00:08:10,720
But you didn't dare to say a word.

112
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:13,160
I dared not speak out of fear
of having my cover blown.

113
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,890
You acted like you got a stroke,

114
00:08:14,980 --> 00:08:16,010
just nodding all along.

115
00:08:16,010 --> 00:08:16,620
Right.

116
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,330
Later on,

117
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:20,430
Baldy Ji got confused.

118
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,340
Finally, he asked you one last question.

119
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,200
He asked, "Whose father are you?"

120
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:28,500
He did.

121
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,960
What was your answer?

122
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,370
Say it. How did you answer him?

123
00:08:31,370 --> 00:08:33,250
I said, "Mr. Ji,

124
00:08:33,250 --> 00:08:36,080
I'm Three Eyes' father, named Four Eyes."

125
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:37,370
Because of you,

126
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:38,789
from that day on,

127
00:08:38,789 --> 00:08:40,669
everyone started calling me Three Eyes.

128
00:08:40,669 --> 00:08:41,480
What were you thinking?

129
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,150
The son of Four Eyes is called Three Eyes?

130
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:45,120
People still refer to me
as Three Eyes now.

131
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,580
Even hookers call me that.

132
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:48,170
And I have to invent a reason,

133
00:08:48,170 --> 00:08:49,750
telling them that in a previous fight,

134
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:50,460
I was wounded

135
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,580
by knives, guns, and firepower.

136
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:53,390
That is complete nonsense.

137
00:08:54,950 --> 00:08:56,210
This is all your fault.

138
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:29,190
How is your sister doing?

139
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:38,450
She underwent surgery.

140
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,150
It was a sucess.

141
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:23,620
Actually, my sister

142
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:27,010
didn't call me until a week

143
00:10:27,530 --> 00:10:28,890
after her surgery.

144
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:34,050
I wasn't happy at all
when I answered the phone,

145
00:10:34,050 --> 00:10:35,910
because I know my sister too well.

146
00:10:36,890 --> 00:10:37,820
If the surgery had failed

147
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:39,250
after such a long time

148
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,600
she spent alone in Shanghai,

149
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,280
she would've had a mental breakdown.

150
00:10:45,630 --> 00:10:46,890
So I got scared at the thought

151
00:10:46,890 --> 00:10:49,150
that the phone call might be from someone

152
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,690
telling me to collect her body.

153
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:58,580
It's okay.

154
00:11:02,580 --> 00:11:03,980
Everything will be fine.

155
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:08,630
Thank you, Brother-in-Law.

156
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:15,760
What "Brother-in-Law"?

157
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,230
I'm not your brother-in-law anymore.

158
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:20,990
You are my brother-in-law.

159
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,610
You treated my sister well.

160
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,050
In fact, I've known the entire time

161
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:29,040
that you got together

162
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,700
with Chen Hong just in order to

163
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,830
earn money for my sister's treatment.

164
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,770
I did hate you at first,

165
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,870
but my sister told me not to.

166
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:40,960
She said to me

167
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,070
that the money for her trip to Shanghai

168
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:45,460
and her surgery

169
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,150
was all from you.

170
00:11:48,870 --> 00:11:51,000
And it was she who suggested a divorce.

171
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:53,910
You already

172
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:56,500
did your utmost by marrying her.

173
00:11:59,550 --> 00:12:01,050
You didn't even learn Chinese well.

174
00:12:01,050 --> 00:12:02,510
Stop using fancy phrases.

175
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,430
I'm serious, Brother-in-Law.

176
00:12:07,530 --> 00:12:10,290
N-Nobody has treated my sister
better than you did.

177
00:12:10,290 --> 00:12:12,550
You treated her better than anyone else.

178
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:29,180
Actually, I've kept one thing...

179
00:12:35,650 --> 00:12:37,390
to myself for a long time.

180
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:56,980
My kidney turned out to be
a match for my sister's.

181
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,940
But I told her it wasn't.

182
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:20,220
When I tore up the test results,

183
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,460
do you know how terrible I felt?

184
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:26,510
I felt like I was a piece of trash.

185
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:31,370
My sister has always been nice to me
since we were little.

186
00:13:31,370 --> 00:13:32,910
But I was scared.

187
00:13:32,910 --> 00:13:34,080
I was just scared.

188
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
When we were kids,

189
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,390
my dad once

190
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:42,010
sent home a bag of White Rabbit candy
from Shanghai.

191
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,520
Every couple of days,

192
00:13:48,050 --> 00:13:50,390
my sister and I would be
each given a piece.

193
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:56,790
But by the time
the whole bag was finished,

194
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:58,990
my sister hadn't eaten a single piece.

195
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:06,080
Then, my mom went mentally ill.

196
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:13,330
Even while my sister was on dialysis,

197
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:15,150
she still cooked for me.

198
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:21,510
But I was just so scared.

199
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:25,050
Sometimes I wonder

200
00:14:25,510 --> 00:14:26,510
why must my sister

201
00:14:26,870 --> 00:14:29,250
be the one who needs dialysis.

202
00:14:33,650 --> 00:14:35,790
Why does she have

203
00:14:35,790 --> 00:14:37,550
such a cowardly brother?

204
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:43,870
Why?

205
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:55,720
Everyone fears death.

206
00:14:59,550 --> 00:15:00,580
I fear death too.

207
00:15:09,170 --> 00:15:11,130
So sometimes, in order to live,

208
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,270
we have to let others die.
